<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Soc Son by Motorbike: Two-Day Trip Planning</h1>
<p>The two-day Soc Son trip is a luxury the district sells cheaply, because a destination this close to the capital rarely deserves the overnight treatment, and yet the temple district rewards exactly that extravagance with the one thing a day trip cannot buy: unhurried time. The overnight shape converts the ride from an errand into a residence, lets the villages be met in their evening and morning moods, and gives the temple calendar the respect of a full circuit. This guide plans the two days without inventing a single hour, price or timetable.</p>
<p>The machines, the briefing and the honest numbers come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk briefs the overnight riders differently than the day trippers. Begin at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, absorb the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/long-distance-motorbike-trip-planning/">long-distance motorbike trip planning</a> guide, see the machines and terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">Why Two Days At All</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">The Shape Of Day One</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">The Overnight Question</a></li>
